  "final_message": "The app is complete and verified. Summary of what I built:\n\n**Backend** (`backend/app.py`): Flask app with token-based auth (SQLite `users`/`sessions`/`previews` tables), password hashing via `werkzeug`, and a preview fetcher using `urllib` + regex to extract `<title>`, `<meta name=\"description\">`, and Open Graph `og:title`/`og:description`/`og:image` (with `og:*` taking precedence). All preview endpoints are user-scoped, newest-first with paging, and 404 for other users' records. Serves the frontend build plus SPA fallback.\n\n**Frontend** (`frontend/`): React + TypeScript with Tailwind CSS v4 (`@tailwindcss/vite`), including sign-in/register, add-link with loading state, preview cards (image, title, description, host), refresh/delete, and paging.\n\n**Verification**: `npm ci` + `npm run build` succeed; a Flask test-client harness passed all API scenarios (auth, duplicate register, 401, OG extraction, isolation, delete, refresh, paging, invalid URL), and gunicorn served `/`, the API, assets, and SPA fallback correctly.\n\nNote: I added `frontend/.gitignore` (ignoring `node_modules/`, `dist/`, and `data/`) since none existed. The Docker build runs `npm ci` and `tsc -b && vite build`, so `tsconfig.json` and the type deps were added to support type-checked builds.",
  "final_message_truncated": false,
